  "id": "COMPOUND:14882 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Chrysaibol appears to have a shared target, CAKI-2, which is also a target of multiple compounds, including 3-Methylhexan-1-ol and Gitoxin. These compounds all ultimately target Phosphodiesterase 6C, suggesting a potential pathway where Chrysaibol may exert its effects through a common mechanism involving CAKI-2. The evidence indicates that Chrysaibol may interact with CAKI-2, which in turn influences Phosphodiesterase 6C, possibly through a direct or indirect interaction. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent and significant relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds targeting Phosphodiesterase 6C, all of which share a common target CAKI-2, supports the hypothesis that Chrysaibol may act through a similar mechanism, potentially modulating the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C.",
